# shooosh

You are working on a WGSL-first site GPU library. WebGPU is the preferred backend; WebGL2 is the fallback. Same scene/item/layer API on both.

Before implementing, read `llms.txt` and `agents.md`, then the next `docs/agent-tasks/` file with `status: todo`. Complete one task per run.

- Author shaders in WGSL (`fsMain`). GLSL 300 es is an escape hatch only. When converting shaders, read `.cursor/skills/wgsl-to-glsl` or `.cursor/skills/glsl-to-wgsl` and `docs/shader-translation.md`. Site mounts/items/post: `docs/site-patterns.md` and the `shooosh-site` / `shooosh-item` / `shooosh-post` skills.
- Source files carry a top “How to use” header. Read that before adding a second API.
- Do not leak `WebGL2RenderingContext` into new public types.
- Shader compile failure: keep last good program, show the log, never blank the page.
- Do not add tensors, Dawn, Three, or a `frame.pass` scene graph.
- Verify with `bun test package` and `bun run bin/build.ts`.
